# =============================================================================
# .env.example  (careeragent-github-mcp)
#
# Copy to .env and paste your token:  cp .env.example .env
# THIS is the only place the GitHub credential lives. careeragent-api never
# holds it. .env is gitignored; only this template is committed.
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GITHUB_PAT — a READ-ONLY GitHub Personal Access Token (fine-grained)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GitHub → Settings → Developer settings → Fine-grained tokens → Generate:
#   - Repository access: All repositories   (your public AND private repos;
#                        pick "Public repositories" instead to exclude private)
#   - Permissions → Repository permissions:
#       Contents  → Read-only
#       Metadata  → Read-only
#     (nothing else)
#
# Read-only is a real guard, and the server also runs with --read-only, so the
# coach can review your repos but can never modify them.
GITHUB_PAT=
